  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Coming back to this after the Avatar Dynamics and OSC update, the \"Report Underage Users\" thread is now the most popular on the VRChat Canny. I think that it is important that the entire moderation and report system should require an overhaul -- also to include the feature of reporting underage users.\nThe report system has been in place since pre-Steam release. The \"Call Moderator\" button was put on the chopping block in mid-2018. The only viable tools that users can perform, are to block, mute, and votekick. Sadly, that doesn't necessarily punish the offending user if they truly are creating a toxic experience for everyone else. Nuisance rank does not seem to be utilized enough.\nAs for a platform like Rec Room, they have active and unpaid volunteer moderators who can forcibly remove and punish troublemakers in the system. They also utilize 'ToxMod' by Modulate to auto-detect hate-speech, and possibly for detecting very underage users. Afterwards, human moderation review the audio logs to determine the appropriate action.\nFor example, if you confirm a report on a user from utilizing their in-platform Report system, you won't receive feedback that action had been taken. On top of that, the only way to truly report a malicious user is through the Zendesk ticketing system that VRChat obscures. The VRChat Trust & Safety team is very reliable, but seem to be very limited.\nAnother problem is that if you report an avatar, it only would only punish the person wearing the avatar, instead of also giving the infraction to the creator of the avatar and taking it down; they get away scott-free. Unoptimized avatars, and sexualized public avatars can become a problem in Quest lobbies where children are present, and I don't want to see the teenage userbase of the platform get exposed to that.\nSummary TL;DR:\n/1.a. Please overhaul the outdated reporting system. More specificities to reporting users, such as being underage, or utilizing modifications.\n/1.b. Make Zendesk tickets more accessible; have them implemented natively in the platform to replace the report system.\n/2. There is no two-way communication between the T&S department and user; we don't even have evidence that the native report system works.\n/3. Offer reliable VRChat users the chance to voluntarily moderate in public lobbies only, to build a more powerful moderation team. Bring back the Call Moderator button; remove the button for those who abuse the button, or have several infractions.",
